// CotSC: English translation extracted from bg0800_baldurs_gate.d
// Original English strings preserved exactly. Translate text inside ~...~ only.

@1 = ~I heard that some brave adventurers cleared the Nashkel mines down south. I commend their courage. It is rare to see genuine virtue in people these days.~
@2 = ~Rumour has it that Aello the Lucky isn't all that lucky. My friend Clarisse bought a scroll of Fire from him, and she ended up having to flee from two aggressive wolves that attacked her upon reading its contents. Someone should notify the Flaming Fist about it. Maybe I will.~
@3 = ~Blast those kobolds to the Hells. In my humble opinion, they should keep away from respectable citizens like us. Who would have thought these mindless creatures would populate the streets with their foul odour?~
@4 = ~You should visit Sorcerous Sundries sometime. Adventurers like you would benefit from the big menagerie of items they sell there.~
@5 = ~Please, be especially careful at night. So many muggers, thieves and other pieces of garbage around. It's baffling. The Flaming Fist has become lazy as of late.~
@6 = ~Watch where you're going!~
@7 = ~Watch where you're going!~
@8 = ~You look the adventurer type. Don't go down the sewer. I'm telling you. The stench of death should be enough to tell you about the gravity of what you might face. Trust me, I'm a kobold.~
@9 = ~Move along. As if there isn't enough rabble in this city. We don't need more of your kind here.~
@10 = ~I have reason to suspect that some storekeepers charge non-humans more. How is it that a human pays one gold coin for a beer, while I pay five? Scandalous.~
@11 = ~Come in to Purple Wyrm Inn behind me! We have drinks, food and rooms. Come in!~
